{
  "chapter": "durability/langgraph-on-temporal",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "The integration runs a graph as a workflow, dispatching each node to an activity or to",
    "workflow code and checkpointing at every node.",
    "Every node must declare execute_in, and it cannot be set as a project-wide default \u2014",
    "explicitly, to prevent determinism bugs. The most consequential decision in the system is",
    "the one the tool refuses to let you skip.",
    "Activities take model calls, I/O, and interrupt(). Workflow nodes take pure transforms,",
    "routing and subgraph orchestration. In a real agent graph almost every node is an",
    "activity; in Atlas exactly one is not, and it is the policy invariant.",
    "Conditional edges always run in the workflow, so a synchronous edge function needs",
    "porting.",
    "The Store is unreachable from an activity node, and it fails at the point of use rather",
    "than at construction.",
    "Below Python 3.11 the plugin loads with a warning rather than failing, so the pause you",
    "built is silently not there.",
    "Temporal's history replaces the LangGraph checkpointer rather than complementing it."
  ],
